<title>UK: Southern Electric firms on H1 results.</title>
<headline>Southern Electric firms on H1 results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Southern Electric firmed 10p to 697-1/2p at 0818 GMT in pre-market trading after the company's interim profits and dividend exceeded market expectations, dealers said.</p>
<p>In releasing its results, the UK electricity provider also said it expected to raise its dividends by five to eight percent in real terms until 2000.</p>
<p>Southern Electric said its pre-tax profits were 112.2 million stg, above the consensus estimate, and issued a dividend of 12.9p per share, which was higher than forecasts.</p>
</text>
